DustyShell_PAH: the multi-bin shell (dustyshell_mulbin) with the two PAH bins drifting as well.
Build with NDUST=4, NPAH=2 (the dustyshell_mulbin Makefile otherwise, NGROUPS=1, RTZ, CALIMA).
Every species starts as the same Gaussian shell (hydro/condinit.f90 :: dustyspress_condinit) and
is pushed by the uniform 8 eV flux of tva_test_mode = TVA_TEST_SPRESS (no force on the gas), so
each drifts at w_k = t_s,k D_k - sum_l eps_l t_s,l D_l, D_k = grad P_g / rho + a_k - sum_l eps_l a_l.
P_g is the Godunov pressure P, uniform here, so the drift is the radiation one. (With the old
P_g = (1 - eps) P, the gradient of eps the 0.1 um shells left across the slower shells moved those
by up to ~10% of their radiation drift: a spurious pressure gradient.)
In 5-10 eV the neutral and ionised PAH cross sections are equal, so the PAH drift does not depend
on the charge state. plot-dustyshell_pah.py predicts every drift from the tables, Epstein drag and
the output gas state (no calibration factor), integrates it over the outputs and compares the
displacement with that of each shell's centroid.
The RTZ chemistry is off (as in dustytrapclump), and the gas is static and isothermal.

&RUN_PARAMS
hydro=.true.
rt=.true.
static=.true.
/

&AMR_PARAMS
levelmin=7
levelmax=8
ngridmax=2000
nparttot=1 
nexpand=1
boxlen=10.0
/

&BOUNDARY_PARAMS
nboundary=2
ibound_min=-1,+1
ibound_max=-1,+1
bound_type= 2, 2
/

&INIT_PARAMS
condinit_kind='dustyspress'
nregion=1
region_type(1)='square'
x_center=5.0
length_x=10.0
d_region=0.204537956
u_region=0.0
p_region=0.14609854
var_region(1,:)=0.0
/

&OUTPUT_PARAMS
noutput=12                    ! every 0.5 Myr: the prediction integrates the drift over the outputs
tout = 0.5,1.0,1.5,2.0,2.5,3.0,3.5,4.0,4.5,5.0,5.5,6.0
tend = 6.0
/

&HYDRO_PARAMS
gamma=1.4
courant_factor=0.8
slope_type=2
riemann='hllc'
data_dir = '/Users/currodri/Documents/RAMSES_dev/rtzdata_for_public_ramses/'
/
&COOLING_PARAMS
    metal = .true.
    cooling = .false.
/

&REFINE_PARAMS
err_grad_d=0.05
err_grad_u=0.05
err_grad_p=0.05
interpol_var=0
interpol_type=2
!err_grad_var(12)=0.05
/

&UNITS_PARAMS
units_length = 3.08567758149137d18 ! 1 pc in cm
units_density = 1e-24 ! 1e-24 g/cm3
units_time = 3.1556926d13 ! 1 Myr in s
/

&RT_PARAMS
rt_flux_scheme='glf'
rt_c_fraction=0.001
rt_otsa=.true.			! no OTSA
rt_is_init_xion=.false.
rt_Tconst=82.831325d0
rt_nsubcycle=518
!----------- RTZ params -----------!
rtz_cooling=.true.             ! the network is off: with it on, rtz_solve_cooling fails in every cell at
                               ! step 0 (so does dustyshell_multbin); the drift test needs none of it
rtz_include_collisional_ionization=.false.
rtz_include_photoionization=.false.
rtz_include_cosmic_ray_ionization=.false.
rtz_include_charge_exchange=.false.
rtz_include_dust_recombination=.false.
rtz_include_HM12_UVB=.false.
isH2_rtz=.false.
isCO_rtz=.false.
rtz_UV_background_G0=1.d0
rtz_primary_cosmic_ray_ionization_rate=1.d-16
rtz_max_cool_timestep=1.d20
!----------- RT Sources -----------!
rt_nsource = 1
rt_source_type(1) = 'square'
rt_exp_source(1) = 10.0
rt_src_x_center(1) = 0.0
rt_src_length_x(1) = 0.625
rt_u_source(1) = 1.0
rt_n_source(1) = 2.5d3
rt_src_group(1) = 1
/

&RT_GROUPS
group_egy     = 8.0
groupL0       = 5.0
groupL1       = 10.0
/

&CALIMA_PARAMS
dust_tva=.true.
dust_radpressure=.true.
use_w_drift_test=.false.
!w_drift_test=0.77692,0.0,0.0
! Chemtype 1: C
dust_composition(1,6) = 1d0

! Chemtype 2: O4MgSiFe
dust_composition(2,8)  = 4d0
dust_composition(2,12) = 1d0
dust_composition(2,14) = 1d0
dust_composition(2,26) = 1d0
dustbins_per_chemtype=2,2
asize=0.01d0,0.1d0,0.005d0,0.1d0 ! Grain size bin centre [microns]
sgrain=2.2d0,2.2d0,3.3d0,3.3d0 ! Grain material density [g/cm^3]
amin = 4d-3,3d-2,1d-3,2d-2 ! Minimum size grain bin [microns]
amax = 3d-2,1d0,2d-2,1d0 ! Maximum size grain bin [microns]

!----------- Grain material parameters -----------!
tensile_strength=2d8,1.5d9
Youngs_modulus=1.0d11,5.4d11
Poisson_ratio=0.32,0.17
surf_energy=75d0,25d0 
work_function=4.4d0,8.0d0 ! [eV]
band_gap=0.0d0,5.0d0 ! [eV]
e_escape_length=1d-7,1d-7 ! [cm]
separate_refractive_index=.true.,.false.
slope_frag_func=0.4333d0

charging_model='Ibanez2019'   ! no charge-dependent process here (Epstein drag; the 5-10 eV PAH cross sections do not depend on the charge)
pah_nc = 54,418                ! PAHBin_01..02 (the H II-slab PAHs)
pah_nc_min = 12,101
pah_nc_max = 101,29952
spah = 2d0,2d0
pah_ncharge_states = 4, 4
dust_tables_dir='/Users/currodri/Documents/RAMSES_dev/rtzdata_for_public_ramses/calima_data/'
/